From 191621e8868c6926fb61889aa7ec48dfe316ff08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO Rung5 <nemo-dev@localhost>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:35:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Rung 5: dynamic-GTODN chemistry Jacobian
 (accretion/LH/photodesorption/H2 sticking)

Complete the analytic grain-abundance Jacobian for the chemistry rate
coefficients that depend on the live grain abundance Y_tot(k) through GTODN
(Rung 5). When a column is a grain population species GRAIN_k^0 / GRAIN_k^-,
the surface-rate coefficients of bin k depend on Y_tot(k) even though GRAIN_k
is not a compound of those reactions, so the standard reactant differentiator
never produces these entries. They are supplied here.

Design: recorded-delta. Each in-scope reaction records its exact
delta = d(reaction_rates)/dY_tot at its rate site (where SUMLAY, the sticking
coefficient, and the floor/cap state are all in scope) into gtodn_jac_dcoef(:)
every RHS evaluation; get_jacobian deposits delta * (bilinear part) into both
charge columns (+w_p to products, -delta*bilinear to reactants). This subsumes
the nu sign, the max(Y_tot,floor) floor, the SUMLAY>=MLAY photodesorption cap
gate, and the H/H2 sticking(SUMLAY) correction in one place, replacing the
static nu/floored metadata (which could not express the sticking wrinkle:
rate ~ Y_tot * stick(SUMLAY(Y_tot)) is not a clean nu=+1 site).

In scope (reduced_CHO fiducial, coagulation on, confounders scope-guarded off):
  - accretion (99): nu=+1
  - Langmuir-Hinshelwood (14): nu=-1, floored (the stiff reciprocal)
  - photodesorption (66/67): nu=+1, floored, monolayer-cap-gated
  - H/H2 accretion sticking: nu=+1 plus slog*dSUMLAY/dY_tot correction
  - LH mantle-multilayer branch: delta=0 (cancellation; v1-inert insurance)

Verified: analytic get_jacobian vs central-difference FD of the RHS, per grain
column, across zero-ice / trace-ice / mild-ice-cap-off / heavy-ice-cap-on
states. With the coagulation kernel isolated (see below) all states agree to
< 1e-5 (worst 3.7e-7), closing gate 5a for the chemistry-coupling entries.
Harness: tests/gtodn_jac_fd_check.{f90,sh}.

KNOWN LIMITATION (-> Rung 5b): full-network 021 != 022 with coagulation on,
failing only on type-50 ice-transport product rows (pre-existing coagulation
Jacobian incompleteness, untouched by this commit; the failing rows are ice on
bins with no chemistry reaction in the perturbed grain's column, where this
commit writes zero). Type-50 was validated at the solution level and ran under
mf=121 through Rung 4, so this is the first application of the entry-exact
021==022 standard to the full network. Production mf stays 121 until 5b lands;
the retarget to 021 is blocked on 5b. See docs/PhaseII_rung5_site_classification.md
section 4 for the record and the working hypothesis (gain-side non-reactant gap).
